:null,"year":null,"weight":15,"yt":null,"src":"ensayos"}],"album_genres":[{"id":147423806094006,"type":"genre","name":"Psychedelic Rock","n":7},{"id":207419651019004,"type":"genre","name":"Garage Rock","n":6},{"id":15604072550254,"type":"genre","name":"Garage Psych","n":6},{"id":185670346256268,"type":"genre","name":"rock","n":4},{"id":141164231500862,"type":"genre","name":"Psychedelic Pop","n":4},{"id":211270792239401,"type":"genre","name":"Roots Rock","n":2},{"id":171871969725315,"type":"genre","name":"Thrash Metal","n":2},{"id":98435208382294,"type":"genre","name":"Boogie Rock","n":2},{"id":276535047502494,"type":"genre","name":"Garage Punk","n":1},{"id":274490571464652,"type":"genre","name":"Noise Rock","n":1},{"id":200232380703960,"type":"genre","name":"Psychedelic Folk","n":1},{"id":194427380844280,"type":"genre","name":"Folk Rock","n":1},{"id":190704175116840,"type":"genre","name":"Progressive Metal","n":1},{"id":190589917177789,"type":"genre","name":"Jam Band","n":1},{"id":190318565344926,"type":"genre","name":"Folk Pop","n":1}],"labels":[],"album_labels":[],"own_scenes":[],"scenes":[],"book_tracks":[],"mentions":[],"podcast":[{"kind":"podcast","title":"Prolific Output and 2017 Album Goal","body":"King Gisart and Elisar Wysart are exceptionally prolific, releasing new material roughly every 8 to 9 months. In 2017, they set an ambitious goal to release five albums within the year, a target considered overwhelming by many. \"Para este 2017 se ponían como objetivo hacer 5 álbumes en un año.\"","year":2017,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"King Gizzard & The Lizard Wizard: ¿Pero que significa Murder of the Universe?","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sIpG7JCrHMU"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Prolific Output in 2017","body":"In 2017, King Gizzard & The Lizard Wizard released four, and possibly five, albums, a feat described as unprecedented. These albums were \"very long,\" \"super distinct,\" and \"super eclectic,\" demonstrating an \"incredible job.\" While not all were equally good, they all maintained a very high minimum quality. \"nunca hemos vivido a alguien hacerse cuatro discos y van a hacer cinco a lo mejor salir quinto y hay cuatro discazos larquísimos súper distintos súper eclecdicos y han hecho un trabajo increíble en este 2017.\"","year":2017,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"Discos que los subsciptores echasteis en falta en la lista de lo mejor del año y tenéis razón","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=APPodZ7sl1w"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Artist in 2010s Psych Resurgence","body":"King Gizzard and the Lizard Wizard was mentioned as one of the artists contributing to the resurgence of Psychedelic or Psych Rock in the 2010s. This genre, which was born in the 1960s and fell out of favor in the 70s, saw a significant comeback during the decade. \"We saw artists like Ariel Pink, King Gizzard and the Lizard Wizard, Temples, the Black Angels, Unknown Mortal Orchestra, Animal Collective, War on Drugs, and Mac DeMarco.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The History of the 2010s Part 4: The Revivals","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HSvgRyGiOpE"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Australian Origin and Rising Popularity","body":"The band is from Australia and, despite having primarily operated within alternative and independent circles, their popularity is rapidly increasing. Their growth is compared to the early stages of Arquit Fayer, a band known for being artistic, eccentric, and independent. \"Es una banda australiana que todavía apenas ha salido de los tírculos alternativos e independientes, pero que la popularidad está creciendo como la espuma.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"King Gizzard & The Lizard Wizard: ¿Pero que significa Murder of the Universe?","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sIpG7JCrHMU"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Complex and Artistic Style","body":"The band is recognized for its highly artistic approach and creation of complex musical pieces. Their album \"Marderoth de Universe\" is cited as an example of their intricate and well-crafted musical compositions. \"King Gisart es un grupo muy arti, que hace cosas verdaderamente complejas.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"King Gizzard & The Lizard Wizard: ¿Pero que significa Murder of the Universe?","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sIpG7JCrHMU"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Detrimental Spoken Word Narration","body":"Despite the album's strong musicality, a significant criticism is directed at the extensive spoken word narrative segments featuring a man and a woman, which are integrated with the sung tracks. These narrative portions are perceived as detracting from the musical experience, overwhelming the otherwise impressive compositions. \"Un hilo argumental musical increíble, potentísimo que se cargan con unas interminables para fadas de gente hablando.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"King Gizzard & The Lizard Wizard: ¿Pero que significa Murder of the Universe?","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sIpG7JCrHMU"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Limited Interviews and Future Clarity","body":"Due to their relatively emerging status, there are very few interviews or public declarations available from the band. It is speculated that a deeper understanding of \"Marderoth de Universe\" and its interconnected stories, particularly regarding the narrative coherence, might only become clear with the release of the third album in their 2017 series. \"Tenemos muy pocas entrevistas de ellos o muy pocas declaraciones de ellos porque todavía no son tan importantes.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"King Gizzard & The Lizard Wizard: ¿Pero que significa Murder of the Universe?","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=sIpG7JCrHMU"}]},{"kind":"podcast","title":"Modern Benchmark for Conceptual Albums","body":"King Gisa Randalizar Wizard are mentioned as a modern example of a band that creates genuinely conceptual albums, serving as a contemporary comparison point for the depth and coherence of conceptual works. \"Álbumes conceptuales modernos como los que puede hacer King Gisa Randalizar Wizard.\"","year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[{"source":"Music Radar Clan","episode":"La discografía de MUSE disco a disco, con lo bueno y con lo malo","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=3Wax146ybgU"}]}],"awards":[],"concerts":[{"kind":"concert","title":"BVC6","body":null,"year":null,"extra":null,"srcs":[]}],"xref":[{"kind":"xref","title":"Artist in 2010s Psych Resurgence","body":"Animal Collective was mentioned as one of the artists contributing to the resurgence of Psychedelic or Psych Rock in the 2010s. This genre, which was born in the 1960s and fell out of favor in the 70s, saw a significant comeback during the decade. \"We saw artists like Ariel Pink, King Gizzard and the Lizard Wizard, Temples, the Black Angels, Unknown Mortal Orchestra, Animal Collective, War on Drugs, and Mac DeMarco.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Animal Collective","from_id":68326050719610,"type":"curiosity"},"srcs":[{"source":"The Ongoing History of New Music","episode":"The History of the 2010s Part 4: The Revivals","url":"https://www.youtube.com/watch?v=HSvgRyGiOpE"}]},{"kind":"xref","title":"Artist in 2010s Psych Resurgence","body":"Ariel Pink was mentioned as one of the artists contributing to the resurgence of Psychedelic or Psych Rock in the 2010s. This genre, which was born in the 1960s and fell out of favor in the 70s, saw a significant comeback during the decade. \"We saw artists like Ariel Pink, King Gizzard and the Lizard Wizard, Temples, the Black Angels, Unknown Mortal Orchestra, Animal Collective, War on Drugs, and Mac DeMarco.\"","year":null,"extra":{"from":"Ariel Pink","from_id":11843700480601,"type":"curiosi